          "By sampling the fast ring oscillator using an independent stable crystal clock, the TRNG captures nondeterministic phase jitter. To comply with NIST SP 800-90B and FIPS 140-3 standards, hardware TRNGs implement continuous Health Tests: (1) The Repetition Count Test (RCT) detects if an oscillator gets stuck at 0 or 1; and (2) The Adaptive Proportion Test (APT) detects statistical bias.",
