          "In elliptic curve cryptography, the most computationally intensive operation is Scalar Multiplication: computing Q = k * P, where k is a secret scalar (such as a device private key) and P is a curve point. The textbook algorithm taught in computer science is the Binary Double-and-Add algorithm: it scans the scalar bits from left to right; for every bit, it doubles the accumulator point (R = 2R); if the bit is 1, it additionally performs a point addition (R = R + P). Step 2: Peripheral asserts RDY & IRQ flags (0xE0) on IOT_SEC_CR1.",
