          "Before any new application firmware or OTA update binary is executed by the microcontroller, the Secure Bootloader must authenticate two fundamental properties: (1) Integrity (proving the image was not corrupted or modified by a bit-flip attack in external SPI Flash); and (2) Authenticity (proving the image was cryptographically signed by the genuine OEM equipment manufacturer). Step 2: Peripheral asserts RDY & IRQ flags (0xE0) on IOT_SEC_CR3.",
