          "Even when cryptographic signature verification is mathematically airtight, embedded systems face a devastating class of attacks known as Firmware Downgrade (Rollback) Attacks. Suppose the OEM discovered a critical remote code execution vulnerability in Firmware Version 1.0 and patched it in Version 2.0. Both versions were legitimately signed with the OEM's master private key! Step 2: Peripheral asserts RDY & IRQ flags (0xE0) on IOT_SEC_CR4.",
